  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Nova Southeastern University (NSU) is a private university in Fort Lauderdale, Florida. Since its founding in 1964, NSU has grown into one of the largest independent universities in the US, providing several undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>NSU offers a diverse campus life with thousands of students from around the globe. Whether you're looking to make new friends or attend fun cultural events, NSU provides numerous opportunities to enhance your student experience, with more than 160 student clubs and organisations.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>The University provides several on-campus housing options with modern facilities. You can choose from double and triple-occupancy rooms, or student apartments too. The University’s housing services team can assist you with finding living spaces to suit your needs and preferences.</p><p>Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\">download our app</a> and check out the Stays feature!</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>The Alvin Sherman Library at NSU is one of the largest libraries in the region. It has a huge collection of books, journals, and digital resources, making it an ideal spot for your studies and research.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>NSU offers several state-of-the-art sports facilities. These include a fitness centre, a swimming pool, and outdoor sports fields. The University competes in basketball, soccer, volleyball, tennis, and more.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>Nova Southeastern University is home to many cutting-edge labs and research facilities. These include specialised labs for health sciences, marine biology, and engineering.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>You have access to several dining venues across the campus. The Razor’s Reef Food Court provides you with various food options, ranging from snacks to healthy meal options and international cuisine. You can also opt for flexible meal plans that fit your needs. You can also grab quick bites from the Supreme Court Café on campus, and other eateries and restaurants nearby.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
